hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16690","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Rabiah ibn Kab al-Aslami, he said: I used to sleep in the chamber of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I would hear him when he rose at night praying, saying: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, for a long while. He said: Then he would say: Glory be to Allah the Tremendous, and with His praise, for a long while."
"16691","He said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, he said: Rabiah ibn Kab al-Aslami narrated to me, he said: I used to spend the night at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), giving him his ablution water. I would hear him after a while of the night saying: Allah hears him who praises Him. And I would hear him after a while of the night saying: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"16692","He said: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Rabiah ibn Kab al-Aslami, he said: I used to spend the night at the door of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), giving him his ablution water. I would hear him after a while of the night saying: Allah hears him who praises Him, and after a while of the night saying: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"16693","He said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: al-Mubarak, meaning Ibn Fadalah, narrated to us, he said: Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Rabiah al-Aslami, he said: I used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Rabiah, will you not marry. He said: I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not wish to marry; I have nothing to maintain a woman, and I dislike anything distracting me from you. He turned from me. I served him what I served him. Then he said to me a second time: O Rabiah, will you not marry. I said: I do not wish to marry; I have nothing to maintain a woman, and I dislike anything distracting me from you. He turned from me. Then I returned to myself and said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knows better than me what is good for me in this world and the Hereafter. By Allah, if he says: Marry, I shall say: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, command me as you wish. He said: He said: O Rabiah, will you not marry. I said: Yes, command me as you wish. He said: Go to the family of so-and-so, a clan of the Ansar, and among them was remissness toward the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Say to them: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to you, ordering you to marry me to so-and-so, a woman among them. I went and said to them: The Messenger of Allah sent me to you, ordering you to marry me to so-and-so. They said: Welcome to the Messenger of Allah and to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). By Allah, the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shall not return except with his need. They married me, treated me kindly, and did not ask me for proof. I returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieved. He said to me: What is the matter with you, O Rabiah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I came to noble people; they married me, honored me, treated me kindly, and did not ask me for proof, and I have no dowry. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Buraydah al-Aslami, gather for him the weight of a date-stone in gold. He said: They gathered for me the weight of a date-stone in gold. I took what they gathered for me and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Go with this to them and say: This is her dowry. I came to them and said: This is her dowry. They accepted it and took it, and said: Much, good. He said: Then I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) grieved. He said: O Rabiah, why are you grieved. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I never saw nobler people than them; they accepted what I brought them, did good, and said: Much, good, and I have nothing for a wedding feast. He said: O Buraydah, gather for him a sheep. He said: They gathered for me a great fat ram. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Go to Aishah and tell her to send the basket in which is food. He said: I came to her and told her what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me. She said: This basket has nine sa of barley; by Allah, we have no food other than it in the morning. Take it. I took it and brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him what Aishah said. He said: Go with this to them and say: Let this be bread with you in the morning. I went to them, and went with the ram, with people from Aslam with me. He said: Let this be bread with you in the morning, and this cooked meat. They said: As for the bread, we shall suffice you of it, and as for the ram, you suffice us of it. We took the ram, I and people from Aslam, slaughtered it, skinned it, and cooked it. In the morning we had bread and meat. I held a wedding feast and invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me land, and Abu Bakr gave me land. Worldly gain came, and we differed over a cluster of a palm tree. I said: It is in my boundary, and Abu Bakr said: It is in my boundary. There were words between me and Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said a word he disliked and regretted. He said to me: O Rabiah, return the like of it to me so it be retaliation. He said: I said: I shall not do. Abu Bakr said: You shall surely say, or I shall seek the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against you. I said: I shall not do. He said: He abandoned the land, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I went following him. People from Aslam came and said to me: May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr; in what does he seek the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against you, while he said to you what he said. I said: Do you know who this is. This is Abu Bakr al-Siddiq. This is the second of two, and this is the elder of the Muslims. Beware, lest he turn and see you aiding me against him, and become angry, and come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he become angry for his anger, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, become angry for their anger, and Rabiah perish. They said: What do you command us. He said: Return. He said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I followed him alone until he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He narrated the account as it was. He raised his head to me and said: O Rabiah, what is the matter between you and al-Siddiq. I said: O Messenger of Allah, it was thus, it was thus. He said to me a word he disliked, and said to me: Say as I said so it be retaliation, and I refused. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, do not return upon him, but say: May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr. I said: May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr. Al-Hasan said: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, turned away weeping."
"16694","He said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Rabiah ibn Kab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Ask me, I shall give you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, grant me time to consider my affair. He said: Consider your affair. He said: I considered and said: The affair of this world ends, and I see nothing better than something I take for myself for my Hereafter. I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is your need. I said: O Messenger of Allah, intercede for me to your Lord, Mighty and Majestic, that He free me from the Fire. He said: Who ordered you with this. I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, none ordered me with it, but I considered my affair and saw that this world passes from its people, and I wished to take for my Hereafter. He said: Help me for yourself with abundant prostration."
"16695","He said: Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata narrated to me, from Nuaym al-Mujmir, from Rabiah ibn Kab, he said: I used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and attend to his needs all my day until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the last Isha. I would sit at his door when he entered his house, saying: Perhaps some need of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) may arise. I kept hearing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah and with His praise, until I grew weary and returned, or my eyes overcame me and I slept. He said: One day he said to me, seeing my readiness for him and my service to him: Ask me, O Rabiah, I shall give you. He said: I said: I shall consider my affair, O Messenger of Allah, then inform you of that. He said: I thought within myself and knew that this world is fleeting, passing, and that I have provision in it that will suffice me and come to me. He said: I said: I shall ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for my Hereafter, for he is with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, in the station he is in. He said: I came, and he said: What did you do, O Rabiah. He said: I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I ask you to intercede for me to your Lord that He free me from the Fire. He said: He said: Who ordered you with this, O Rabiah. He said: I said: No, by Allah who sent you with the truth, none ordered me with it, but when you said: Ask me, I shall give you, and you are with Allah in the station you are in, I considered my affair and knew that this world is fleeting and passing, and that I have provision in it that will come to me. I said: I shall ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for my Hereafter. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent long, then said to me: I shall do, so help me for yourself with abundant prostration."
